# 💰 My Finance Tracker

A lightweight personal finance tracker built entirely on **Google Sheets, Google Forms, and Google Apps Script** — no external database or hosting required.

Log expenses, income, transfers, lending, borrowing, and investments in a few seconds from any device (including mobile), and see everything automatically organized into monthly sheets with a live, filterable dashboard.

## Features

- 📝 **Simple entry form** (Google Form) — works on desktop and mobile, no app install needed
- 📅 **Automatic monthly sheets** — each transaction is filed into the correct month's sheet (e.g. `Sep-2026`) based on the transaction date, not just the submission date
- 🔄 **Smart date handling** — leave the date blank to default to today, or enter a past date and it's correctly filed under that month
- 📊 **Live Dashboard** — auto-updating summary of total income, expenses, savings, and breakdowns by category, account, payment method, and expense nature
- 🔍 **Filterable trends** — dropdown filters for Year and Category, showing:
  - Filtered totals (expenses, income, net)
  - Month-by-month trend for the selected year
  - Year-over-year trend for the selected category
- 🧾 **Categorized transactions** — expense category, account/wallet, payment method, fixed vs. variable, recurring flag, and free-form notes
- 🗂️ **Invoice item detail sheets** (`_Items`) — structure in place for itemized invoice/receipt breakdowns
- ⚙️ **One-time setup** — a single script run creates the form, sheets, dashboard, and trigger; safe to re-run without duplicating anything

## How it works

1. `setupFinanceTracker()` is run once from the Apps Script editor attached to a Google Sheet.
2. It creates:
   - A Google Form ("💰 My Finance Tracker") with all transaction fields
   - Supporting sheets: `Dashboard`, `Settings`, `Categories`, `Accounts`
   - A form-submit trigger that processes each response automatically
3. On every form submission:
   - The transaction date and amount are parsed and validated
   - A unique Transaction ID is generated
   - The entry is appended to that month's transaction sheet (created automatically if it doesn't exist yet)
   - The Dashboard and filtered trend views refresh automatically

## Tech stack

- **Google Apps Script** (JavaScript, V8 runtime)
- **Google Forms** — data entry
- **Google Sheets** — storage, reporting, and dashboard
- Uses `FormApp`, `SpreadsheetApp`, `PropertiesService`, and installable/simple triggers (`onFormSubmit`, `onEdit`)

## Setup (about 5 minutes, no coding needed)

### 1. Create a new Google Sheet
Go to [sheets.google.com](https://sheets.google.com) and create a blank spreadsheet. The name doesn't matter, because the script renames it to "My Finance Tracker".

### 2. Open Apps Script
In the Sheet, click **Extensions → Apps Script**. A new tab opens with the script editor.

### 3. Paste the code
- Delete everything in the default `Code.gs` file.
- Paste in the full contents of `FinanceTracker_v3.gs` from this repo.
- Click the **Save** icon (or press Ctrl+S).

### 4. Check the time zone
- In Apps Script, open **Project Settings** (gear icon) and confirm the **Time zone** matches yours.
- In the Sheet, open **File → Settings** and confirm the same time zone there.

This keeps transactions from landing in the wrong month near month boundaries.

### 5. Run the setup
- In the function dropdown at the top of the editor, select **`setupFinanceTracker`**.
- Click **Run**.

### 6. Authorize the permissions
Google shows an authorization popup the first time. Because this is your own personal script, you will see an "unverified app" warning. That is expected. Click through:

**Review permissions → choose your account → Advanced → Go to [project name] (unsafe) → Allow**

The script needs access to Sheets and Forms to create the form, write monthly sheets, and run the submit trigger.

### 7. Wait for it to finish
Setup can take 1-2 minutes. When it finishes, an alert appears in your **Sheet tab** saying "Finance Tracker Setup Completed!" Switch to the Sheet tab and click **OK**, because the script stays paused until you dismiss the alert.

### 8. Get your form link
Either of these works:
- In the Sheet, use the **💰 Finance Tracker → Open Finance Form** menu (refresh the page if the menu isn't there yet).
- In Apps Script, open **Executions**, click the `setupFinanceTracker` run, and copy the `Google Form URL` line from the log.

### 9. Put the form on your phone
- Email or message the link to yourself and open it on your phone.
- In Chrome, use **⋮ → Add to Home screen** for a one-tap shortcut.

### Optional: invoice photo upload
Apps Script cannot create File Upload questions, so add one manually in the Form editor if you want it:
- Add a question of type **File upload**.
- Title it exactly **`Bill / Invoice Photo`**, because the script matches on that name.
- Respondents will then need to be signed in to Google to submit.

## Usage

- **Date field:** leave it blank to use today, or pick a past date and the entry goes into that month's sheet (e.g. `Aug-2026`).
- **Dashboard:** open the **Dashboard** tab and use the **Year** and **Category** dropdowns in columns J-K to view filtered totals, monthly trends, and yearly trends.
- **Manual refresh:** use **💰 Finance Tracker → Refresh Dashboard** or **Refresh Filtered Dashboard** if anything looks stale.

## Troubleshooting

| Problem | Fix |
|---|---|
| Form submits but no monthly sheet appears | Check **Apps Script → Executions** for a failed `processFinanceTransaction` run and read the error |
| "Invalid amount" error | Make sure the Amount field contains a plain number (e.g. `250`) |
| Menu doesn't appear | Refresh the Sheet page |
| Setup times out | Run `setupFinanceTracker` again. It is safe to re-run and won't duplicate the form |
| Changed the script but the form looks unchanged | Run `updateExistingFormDescriptions` to patch descriptions onto the existing form |
| "Run" seems stuck with only "Execution started" | An alert is waiting in the Sheet tab. Switch to it and click **OK** |

